    "id": "trump-holds-talks-separately-with-putin-8382ca38",
    "title": "Trump holds talks separately with Putin and Xi ahead of their historic trilateral meeting",
    "titleJa": "Trump holds talks separately with Putin and Xi ahead of their historic trilateral meeting",
    "summaryJa": "U.S. President Donald Trump met individually on Thursday with Russian President Vladimir Putin, as well as Chinese President Xi Jinping.",
    "bodyOriginal": "SHENZHEN, China — U.S. President Donald Trump met with Vladimir Putin and Xi Jinping separately on Thursday, ahead of a scheduled trilateral with his Russian and Chinese counterparts, according to pool notes and Chinese state media.\nEarlier on Thursday, the leaders and other members of the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation gathered for a summit. Trump and Xi entered the room side by side.\nXi said China would provide $20 million to support APEC cooperation, and establish a \"Center for Asia-Pacific Community Studies in Shenzhen to conduct policy research and exchanges and provide intellectual support.\"\nLater in the morning session, Trump said that he opposed regulating artificial intelligence as it would \"stifle\" the industry.\n\"The United States has been a Pacific power for hundreds of years, and we continue to work to promote growth and stability, sovereignty, prosperity, and peace throughout this region,\" Trump said.\nU.S. officials said last week that Trump did not plan to raise Nvidia's Jensen Huang and allegations of an affair with a Chinese spy at his meetings.\n\"By hosting APEC in Shenzhen, China took the opportunity to showcase another of its economic powerhouse cities, this time one that is home to some of the country's leading technology companies and innovators,\" AmCham China President Michael Hart said.\n\"The scale of China's economic strength and technological ambition is clear to U.S. businesses,\" he said. \"They recognize the importance of the Chinese market, but also understand that they need to remain competitive, innovative, and prepared to compete in an increasingly sophisticated business environment.\"",
    "bodyJa": "SHENZHEN, China — U.S. President Donald Trump met with Vladimir Putin and Xi Jinping separately on Thursday, ahead of a scheduled trilateral with his Russian and Chinese counterparts, according to pool notes and Chinese state media.\nEarlier on Thursday, the leaders and other members of the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation gathered for a summit. Trump and Xi entered the room side by side.\nXi said China would provide $20 million to support APEC cooperation, and establish a \"Center for Asia-Pacific Community Studies in Shenzhen to conduct policy research and exchanges and provide intellectual support.\"\nLater in the morning session, Trump said that he opposed regulating artificial intelligence as it would \"stifle\" the industry.\n\"The United States has been a Pacific power for hundreds of years, and we continue to work to promote growth and stability, sovereignty, prosperity, and peace throughout this region,\" Trump said.\nU.S. officials said last week that Trump did not plan to raise Nvidia's Jensen Huang and allegations of an affair with a Chinese spy at his meetings.\n\"By hosting APEC in Shenzhen, China took the opportunity to showcase another of its economic powerhouse cities, this time one that is home to some of the country's leading technology companies and innovators,\" AmCham China President Michael Hart said.\n\"The scale of China's economic strength and technological ambition is clear to U.S. businesses,\" he said. \"They recognize the importance of the Chinese market, but also understand that they need to remain competitive, innovative, and prepared to compete in an increasingly sophisticated business environment.\"",
    "source": "CNBC",
    "sourceUrl": "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/19/trump-xi-putin-china-apec-.html",
    "publishedAt": "2026-11-19T06:29:34+00:00",
    "category": "テクノロジー",
    "imageUrl": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518770660439-4636190af475?w=800&q=80",
    "readTime": 4
